{
  "dom_id": "step-q84114",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[2A+5B]$ if $\\text{E}[A]=-0.5$ and $\\text{E}[B]=0.4.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2A+5B] & =2\\text{E}[A]+5\\text{E}[B] \\\\  & =2(-0.5)+5(0.4) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
